        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Thought it would be an easly A I was wrong. Exams seem to be graded randomly, and it's difficult to understand how final scores are determined. He does not stay after class to answer questions, and communication outside of class is frustrating I had to email him multiple times just to get a response! Grades are also posted very late! DO NOT TAKE. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 1
            },
            {
                "comment": "Wodzynski was the best! His lectures were so interesting, funny, and well-organized. He clearly cared about his students and wanted them to do well in the course. There were 4-question reading quizzes about the material, three exams, and one final group project. If you pay attention during lecture, do the readings/movies, you will get an A. \n",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "(Littrans 215)  He only talks the entire lecture and has \"Archeological Notes\" that he randomly grades and then comments question marks with no other feedback. He also never puts in grades so you won't know your grade till the end of the semester. And you cant use the feedback he gives you, because he is so behind on grading the notes. ",
